###############################################################################
# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# Efficiency on a single NVIDIA A100 (SXM4, 40 GB), in seconds per MC
# step (Table 1): MACE-MP-0a 0.0081, MACE-MP-0b3 0.0231, MACE-MPA-0 0.0279,
# ORB-v3 0.0167, fairchem ODAC23 0.0556, ODAC25 0.1431. The system size
# of the timing is not stated, so no per-atom time is derived.

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - Accuracy is assessed through isosteric heats and isotherms relative to a fine-tuned reference model of Goeminne et al., which are not accuracy metrics of the schema.
# - The fairchem ODAC23 and ODAC25 models are described only as graph transformers; they are not encoded as runs.
# - MLIP-MC (introduced here) is a simulation framework that drives MLIP calculators through ASE; it is not an implementation of an MLIP method and has no node in the schema.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: datacite).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/edwards2026.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.
